Empirical Findings:
  1. Root cause of the ~12% compute-heavy gap is measured and confirmed:
     MiniPTX runtime matches the no-FMA CUDA control exactly (0.4424 ms vs 0.4424 ms, 1.000x).
     Default FMA fusion in nvcc accounts for the entire 12% gap.
  2. Absolute execution times vary across runs on the shared DGX cluster (e.g. 0.4424 ms vs 0.4721 ms),
